    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "552840d6_49cd6f36",
        "filename": "util/ec_flash.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 115,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-07-01T17:58:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why are we deprecating only v1 instead of v0 and v1?",
      "parentUuid": "65292750_e947ecc9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 113,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 115,
        "endChar": 43
      },
      "revId": "592d44c625188e4d383e7ac57bec4f20b6de0170",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "eb58c9e1_e9a8e288",
        "filename": "util/ec_flash.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 115,
      "author": {
        "id": 1314845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-07-01T18:31:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In my mind this isn\u0027t deprecating anything. It\u0027s adding support for the v2 command. If someone wants to add support and test the v1 command, the code is written in a way to make that easy. Incremental improvements to the code shouldn\u0027t force me to fix all the problems that others have introduced in the past (i.e., this should have been added when the command was added).",
      "parentUuid": "552840d6_49cd6f36",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 113,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 115,
        "endChar": 43
      },
      "revId": "592d44c625188e4d383e7ac57bec4f20b6de0170",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3585376f_16f6b991",
        "filename": "util/ec_flash.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 115,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-07-01T18:54:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we\u0027re not supporting v1, do we have to support v0? Is it clear from user\u0027s perspective, if v2 isn\u0027t supported, the command falls back to v0 (instead of v1)?\n\nFrom what I read the code, we can always call v0 because it can return write_size. Can you clarify why it has to be v2?",
      "parentUuid": "eb58c9e1_e9a8e288",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 113,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 115,
        "endChar": 43
      },
      "revId": "592d44c625188e4d383e7ac57bec4f20b6de0170",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9a460efd_6ec3d7f0",
        "filename": "util/ec_flash.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 115,
      "author": {
        "id": 1314845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-07-11T21:30:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We don\u0027t have to support v0. I was just being cautious and trying not to break anyone that is relying on it.\n\nIn my case, I was trying to reproduce an issue that I was seeing with the STM32F412 when using flashrom. It was somewhat hard to debug with flashrom, so I wanted to use ectool to repro, which required using the same EC_CMD_FLASH_INFO version as flashrom).\n\nWould you prefer to remove the v0 command completely from ectool?",
      "parentUuid": "3585376f_16f6b991",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 113,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 115,
        "endChar": 43
      },
      "revId": "592d44c625188e4d383e7ac57bec4f20b6de0170",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
